{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 26, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler to Japan's land of wonder\nThy journey shall begin on a noble date\nDay one shall dawn upon thy arrival in Tokyo\nAt Narita or Haneda airport where thou shalt take\nA train to Shinjuku and thy hotel there reside\nThe next day thou shalt venture forth to Senso-ji\nA temple of old where cherry blossoms bloom\nIn Ueno Park thou shalt stroll and take in the sights\nAnd sample the local cuisine of tempura and sushi\n\nDay three thou shalt make thy way to Asakusa\nWhere the famous Nakamise shopping street doth lie\nThou shalt browse the stalls and buy souvenirs to take home\nAnd visit the Kanda Shrine where the gods do reside\nIn the evening thou shalt dine at a yakitori bar\nAnd sample the local delicacy of grilled chicken\n\nDay four thou shalt travel to Kyoto the city of peace\nAnd visit the Fushimi Inari shrine where thousands of torii gates do stand\nThou shalt hike the famous orange torii gates trail\nAnd take in the breathtaking views of the city below\nIn the evening thou shalt attend a traditional tea ceremony\nAnd sample the local sweets and Japanese snacks\n\nDay five thou shalt visit the Kiyomizu-dera temple\nA UNESCO world heritage site and one of Japan's most famous\nThou shalt take in the stunning views of the city below\nAnd visit the nearby Nijo Castle a masterpiece of Japanese architecture\nIn the evening thou shalt return to Tokyo and prepare for departure\n\nFair traveler may this itinerary serve thee well\nAnd guide thee through the wonders of Japan's land so fair\nMay thy journey be filled with joy and delight\nAnd may thy memories of Japan last forevermore.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Fair", "logprob": -0.0058578010648489}, {"token": " traveler", "logprob": -0.008872726000845432}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -1.5376625061035156}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -0.0017532228957861662}, {"token": "'s", "logprob": -0.28012248